{"conversation":"Thanks for the hint! I will try sorting batteries first and then try to apply some checks for feasibility of running for time t. I think I can use binary search on time to find the maximum possible time all computers can run. I will write code to start this idea.","python_code":"class Solution:
    def maxRunTime(self, n: int, batteries: List[int]) -> int:
        batteries.sort()
        left, right = 1, sum(batteries) // n

        def can_run(t):
            total = 0
            for b in batteries:
                total += min(b, t)
            return total >= t * n

        while left < right:
            mid = (left + right + 1) // 2
            if can_run(mid):
                left = mid
            else:
                right = mid - 1
        return left"}
